WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.148
Poly(lactic acid) may keep its familiar bulk chemistry

00:00:04.148 --> 00:00:07.270
while the interface that meets its environment

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:07.813
changes.

00:00:11.717 --> 00:00:15.340
Cold plasma can activate a polymer surface, opening

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.177
opportunities for grafting chemistry without replacing

00:00:19.177 --> 00:00:21.380
the entire underlying material.

00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:30.117
Our coauthored research examined grafting approaches

00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:33.866
involving fumaric and ascorbic acids on PLA films,

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.866
connecting surface chemistry to material

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:38.141
characterisation.

00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:47.402
Morphology and chemical characterisation can tell

00:00:47.402 --> 00:00:47.905
whether

00:00:47.905 --> 00:00:51.574
a proposed surface transformation is consistent with

00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:53.621
observed material properties.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:01.911
The biologically relevant encounter happens at an

00:01:01.911 --> 00:01:05.707
interface. A changed surface does not itself establish

00:01:05.707 --> 00:01:07.746
performance inside a patient.

00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:15.956
This study illustrates how targeted chemistry can

00:01:15.956 --> 00:01:16.393
change

00:01:16.393 --> 00:01:19.893
the questions a biodegradable polymer is able to

00:01:19.893 --> 00:01:20.403
answer.
